    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This thesis seeks to provide clarity around how gender impacts human perceptions of\r\nVAs. The thesis consists of two parts: a scholarly literature review and an in-lab empirical study.\r\nIn the literature review, I review relevant work to show the importance of anthropomorphism in\r\nHCI research and the specific importance of gender as a determinant for how humans interact\r\nwith and perceive digital technologies. In the second part, I present the results of an in-lab\r\nempirical study that I conducted to understand whether interacting with gendered VAs has an\r\neffect on attitudes towards VAs, focusing on warmth and competence, perceptions of\r\nanthropomorphism, and mood.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
